                "event": "Marine Weather Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Marine Weather Statement issued November 15 at 3:13AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "A moderate, long-period north swell from 350 to 360 degrees will\nbuild across Hawaiian waters and peak later today and Monday as\nthe period shortens to 12 seconds. The swell will produce\nmoderate to heavy surges in north-facing harbors, especially at\nKahului and Hilo Harbors. Mariners using these harbors should\nexercise caution when mooring or launching vessels and when\nentering or leaving port. The swell will diminish Tuesday.",
                "instruction": null,
                "response": "Monitor",
