                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 15 at 4:10AM AKST until November 15 at 12:00PM AKST by NWS Juneau AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Northeast winds 15 to 30 mph with gusts up to 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Downtown Juneau, Thane, and Douglas\n\n* WHEN...Until noon AKST today.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A mountain wave strong wind event is ongoing\nbetween Downtown Juneau and Thane, with localized gusts near the AJ\nDock and AML Dock around 45 mph. Frequent gusts to 30 mph with\nsporadic wind gusts up to 40 mph will be possible for the Downtown\nJuneau, Thane, and Douglas areas through Sunday morning before\ndiminishing.",
