                "description": "* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 22 to 25 feet with sets up to 28\nfeet possible.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal Del Norte, Northern Coastal Humboldt,\nSouthwestern Humboldt and Coastal Mendocino Counties.\n\n* WHEN...From noon today to 4 AM PST Monday. .\n\n* IMPACTS...Dangerous surf conditions and localized beach\nerosion. Beachcombing is highly discouraged!.",
                "instruction": "Large breaking waves along the coast will lead to increased wave\nrun-up on beaches with waves topping and washing over large rocks\nand jetties. These large waves can be erratic and unpredictable.\nUse extra caution near the surf zone as these large waves will be\ncapable of sweeping people into the frigid and turbulent ocean\nwater. Mariners traversing the bar are urged to exercise extreme\ncaution or stay in port until the threat subsides. Please contact\nthe U.S. Coast Guard for information regarding harbor and bar\nclosures.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "CFWEKA"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WHUS46 KEKA 151307"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "HIGH SURF ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM NOON TODAY TO 4 AM PST MONDAY"
                    ],
                    "BLOCKCHANNEL": [
                        "EAS",
                        "NWEM",
                        "CMAS"
                    ],
                    "VTEC": [
