                "urgency": "Expected",
                "event": "High Wind Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "High Wind Warning issued November 15 at 3:58AM AKST until November 17 at 6:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Southwest winds 45 to 60 mph with gusts as high as 80 mph\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Atka and Adak.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM Monday to 6 AM AKST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High winds may move loose debris, damage property, and\ncause power outages. Travel will be difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strongest winds are will be over Adak,\nwith wind gusts as high as 80 mph, with Atka winds expected to see\ngusts to 60 mph. Winds rapidly increase in strength late Monday\nevening and peak early Tuesday morning as a strong low pressure\nsystem moves through the Bering. Winds will gradually lighten but\nremain gusty through Wednesday.",
                "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind. Prepare for the possibility of widespread\npower outages. Use caution if you must drive.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "NPWALU"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
