                "description": "Offshore Waters Forecast for the US Arctic Waters\n\nSea forecasts represent an average of the highest one-third of\nthe combined wind wave and swell height. Individual waves may be\ntwice as high.\n\n.TODAY...E winds 40 kt. Seas 15 ft. Snow in the morning. Blowing\nsnow through the day. Extreme freezing spray.\n.TONIGHT...E winds 30 kt with gusts to around 45 kt. Seas 10 ft.\nBlowing snow. Snow. Extreme freezing spray.\n.MON...E winds 30 kt with gusts to around 45 kt. Seas 9 ft.\nBlowing snow. Snow. Extreme freezing spray.\n.MON NIGHT...E winds 30 kt. Seas 7 ft. Blowing snow. Snow.\nExtreme freezing spray.\n.TUE...E winds 30 kt. Seas 4 ft.\n.WED...E winds 30 kt. Seas 7 ft.\n.THU...E winds 30 kt. Seas 9 ft.",
                "instruction": null,
                "response": "Avoid",
