                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 15 at 2:37AM HST until November 15 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "* WHAT...East winds 15 to 30 mph with gusts up to 50 mph are\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of Oahu, Molokai, Lanai, Kahoolawe, Maui, and the\nBig Island of Hawaii.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Winds this strong can tear off shingles, knock down tree\nbranches, blow away tents and awnings and make it difficult to\nsteer, especially for drivers of high profile vehicles.",
                "instruction": "Watch out for falling tree branches when walking or driving. Make\nsure tents and awnings are secure or take them down. Be prepared for\npower outages.\n\nUse extra caution when driving, especially if operating a high\nprofile vehicle. Secure outdoor objects.",
