                "severity": "Moderate",
                "certainty": "Likely",
                "urgency": "Expected",
                "event": "High Surf Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Medford OR",
                "headline": "High Surf Warning issued November 15 at 4:08AM PST until November 16 at 10:00PM PST by NWS Medford OR",
                "description": "* WHAT...Breaking waves 15 to 20 feet this morning. Conditions\nworsen this afternoon with breaking waves reaching 25 to 30 ft.\nDangerous surf conditions persist into Monday morning. Waves\nand surf remain hazardous Monday, but gradually diminish through\nMonday evening.\n\n* WHERE...Beaches of South Central Oregon Coast and Curry County\nCoast. This includes Charleston, Port Orford, Gold Beach, and\nBrookings.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM PST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Extremely large breaking waves will create very\nhazardous conditions along beaches and area shorelines. Waves\nwill inundate beaches and surge into normally dry areas.\nInfrastructure damage and significant beach erosion can be\nexpected.",
                "instruction": "Beaches and coastlines will become dangerous due to very large\nand life-threatening surf conditions. Stay off of beaches, rocks,\njetties, piers, and other waterside infrastructure.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "CFWMFR"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WHUS46 KMFR 151208"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
