                "event": "Beach Hazards Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued November 15 at 6:07AM CST until November 16 at 12:00PM CST by NWS Houston/Galveston TX",
                "description": "* WHAT...High risk of rip currents. Minor coastal flooding\npossible around high tide times today into Monday.\n\n* WHERE...Gulf-facing beaches, including the Matagorda\nPeninsula, Brazoria County beaches, Galveston Island and the\nBolivar Peninsula.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Rip currents can sweep even the best swimmers away\nfrom shore into deeper water. Strong winds and elevated seas\nwill drive wave runup further up the beach than is typically\nnormal. There is a risk of minor coastal flooding along the\nlow lying areas from the Bolivar Peninsula to Surfside around\nhigh tide times today into Monday.",
                "instruction": "Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "CFWHGX"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WHUS44 KHGX 151207"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
