                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 15 at 4:06AM PST until November 15 at 1:00PM PST by NWS Medford OR",
                "description": "* WHAT...South winds 25 to 35 mph with gusts up to 55 mph expected.\n\n* WHERE...Most of the Shasta Valley in central Siskiyou County. This\nincludes portions of Interstate 5 as well as the communities of\nWeed, Gazelle, Grenada and Montague.\n\n* WHEN...Until 1 PM PST this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and driving may become difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Highways running west to east will be exposed\nto tough driving conditions given the strong southerly wind speeds.",
                "instruction": "Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles. Use extra caution.\n\nPeople are urged to secure loose objects, including large or\ninflatable holiday decorations that could be blown around or damaged\nby the wind.",
                "response": "Execute",
