                "description": "A large west to northwesterly swell will continue to produce\nbreaking waves at the Morro Bay and Ventura Harbor entrances\nthrough at least this afternoon. These conditions have a history\nof capsizing vessels of various sizes resulting in serious injury\nor death, even to the most experienced mariners. Mariners are\nurged to stay clear of these harbor entrances. For more\ninformation, contact the local harbor patrol or coast guard\nstation and continue to monitor NOAA Weather Radio for the latest\nweather information.",
                "instruction": null,
                "response": "Monitor",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "MWSLOX"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "FZUS76 KLOX 151126"
                    ],
                    "BLOCKCHANNEL": [
                        "EAS",
                        "NWEM",
                        "CMAS"
                    ]
                },
                "scope": "Public",
                "code": "IPAWSv1.0",
                "language": "en-US",
