                "severity": "Moderate",
                "certainty": "Likely",
                "urgency": "Expected",
                "event": "High Surf Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "headline": "High Surf Warning issued November 15 at 3:24AM PST until November 15 at 4:00PM PST by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...For the High Surf Warning, dangerously large breaking\nwaves of 14 to 18 feet with dangerous rip currents. For the High\nSurf Advisory, large breaking waves of 10 to 15 feet with\ndangerous rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...San Luis Obispo County Beaches and Santa Barbara\nCounty Central Coast Beaches.\n\n* WHEN...For the High Surf Warning, until 4 PM PST this\nafternoon. For the High Surf Advisory, from 4 PM this\nafternoon to 3 PM PST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Powerful waves and strong rip currents will pose an\nexceptional risk of ocean drowning and damage to coastal\nstructures like piers and jetties. Large breaking waves can\ncause injury, wash people off beaches and rocks, and capsize\nsmall boats near shore.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A series of west-northwesterly swells will\ncreate an extended period of large surf into the week, with the\npotential for WARNING level surf again late tonight through\nMonday. Areas that may see most significant impacts will be\nwest- northwest facing beaches, with widespread flooding likely\nat low lying areas such as at Oceano Dunes. Breaking waves may\nimpact the Cayucos and Pismo Beach piers as well as the Morro\nBay Harbor entrance.",
                "instruction": "Everyone should remain out of the water due to life-threatening\nsurf conditions. Stay off of jetties, piers, and other water side\ninfrastructure.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "CFWLOX"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WHUS46 KLOX 151124"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "HIGH SURF WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 4 PM PST THIS AFTERNOON... ...HIGH SURF ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4 PM THIS AFTERNOON TO 3 PM PST TUESDAY"
                    ],
                    "BLOCKCHANNEL": [
                        "EAS",
                        "NWEM",
                        "CMAS"
                    ],
                    "VTEC": [
                        "/O.NEW.KLOX.SU.W.0002.261115T1124Z-261116T0000Z/"
                    ],
                    "eventEndingTime": [
