                "event": "High Surf Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
                "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 15 at 12:51AM PST until November 18 at 4:00AM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 5 to 7 feet with sets 8 to 10\nfeet along west-facing beaches and very strong rip currents.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 AM PST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Dangerous swimming and surfing conditions and\nlocalized beach erosion.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...While surf gradually wanes today into\nMonday, it will still remain elevated (4-7 feet). A fresh swell\narrives Monday afternoon, ramping the surf heights back up to 5\nto 7 feet, with sets to 8-9 feet along west-facing beaches.",
                "instruction": "Inexperienced swimmers should remain out of the water due to\ndangerous surf conditions.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
