                "senderName": "NWS Corpus Christi TX",
                "headline": "Gale Warning issued November 14 at 11:59PM CST until November 16 at 6:00PM CST by NWS Corpus Christi TX",
                "description": "* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, southeast winds 15 to 25\nknots and seas 5 to 8 feet. For the Gale Warning, northeast\nwinds 25 to 30 knots with gusts up to 40 knots and seas 8 to 13\nfeet expected.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal waters from Baffin Bay to Port Aransas out 20\nNM, Coastal waters from Port Aransas to Matagorda Ship Channel\nout 20 NM, Waters from Baffin Bay to Port Aransas from 20 to\n60 NM and Waters from Port Aransas to Matagorda Ship Channel\nfrom 20 to 60 NM.\n\n* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until midnight CST Sunday\nnight. For the Gale Warning, from midnight Sunday night to 6\nPM CST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gale force winds and high seas will result in\ndangerous marine conditions which could result in capsized or\ndamaged vessels.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Gale force winds may arrive earlier if the\nfront continues to trend faster.",
                "instruction": "Mariners should consider altering plans to avoid possible\nhazardous conditions.  Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter\ncourse, and/or secure the vessel for severe wind and seas.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "MWWCRP"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WHUS74 KCRP 150559"
