                "description": "Southeast Alaska Inside Waters from Dixon Entrance to Skagway\n\nWind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction\nexpected. Sea forecasts represent the average of the highest\none-third of the combined windwave and swell height.\n\nUPDATED\n\n...GALE WARNING THROUGH LATE SUNDAY...\n\n.REST OF TONIGHT...E wind 30 kt becoming SE 45 kt late. Seas 9 ft\nbuilding to 14 ft. Rain.\n\n.SUN...SE wind 40 kt. Gusts to 55 kt, except 45 kt out of\ninterior passes. Seas 15 ft. Rain in the afternoon.\n.SUN NIGHT...S gale to 35 kt. Gusts to 45 kt out of interior\npasses. Seas 15 ft. Rain.\n.MON...S wind 30 kt. Gusts to 45 kt. Seas 11 ft, except 14 ft\nnear ocean entrances. Rain.\n.MON NIGHT...SE gale to 35 kt. Gusts to 50 kt. Seas 10 ft,\nexcept 13 ft near ocean entrances. Rain.\n.TUE...SE gale to 35 kt. Seas 9 ft.\n.WED...SE wind 10 kt. Seas 4 ft.\n.THU...SE gale to 40 kt. Seas 5 ft.",
